      "side": 1,
      "message": "When creating SubRuns there are no empty glyphs; those are dropped much higher in the stack. So higher in the drawing stack this can happen if the size is extremely large, but this would result in empty SubRuns.  \n\nI think you are correct about the size max being 65536. I will adjust the code accordingly to use 65536 instead.\n\nI performed the following experiment. I changed scaledemoji to only have the 340 size blob. Then in viewer, use real perspective, and make an extreme keystone. Start pressing the up arrow. I have instrumented to print the matrix, the font size, and the font size * scaleX at 3053. At 3049, I set a flag to true. At 3066 I print the fully precondition matrix, and break if the flat is set.\n\nHere is the output:\n\nBefore precondition:\n[107.6516   0.0000   0.0000][  0.0000 107.6516   0.0000][  0.0000   0.0000   1.0000]\nFont size: 340 Estimate: 36601.5\nAfter precondition:\n[  0.9228   0.0000   0.0000][  0.0000   0.9228   0.0000][  0.0000   0.0000   1.0000]\nBefore precondition:\n[180.2092   0.0000   0.0000][  0.0000 180.2092   0.0000][  0.0000   0.0000   1.0000]\nFont size: 340 Estimate: 61271.1\nIt\u0027s happening\nAfter precondition:\n[  0.9252   0.0000   0.0000][  0.0000   0.9252   0.0000][  0.0000   0.0000   1.0000]\n../../src/text/gpu/SubRunContainer.cpp:3085: fatal error: \"Oh no\n\"\nfish: Job 1, \u0027./out/Debug/viewer --backend...\u0027 terminated by signal SIGILL (Illegal instruction)\n\n\nSo, we get a zero from the max dimension when font size * scaleX (340 * 180.2092) is 61271.1 which is very close to 65536.",
